It fixes up L4 checksums via `csum_diff` and `l4_csum_replace`, then swaps the MACs — loading the source MAC and storing it as destination, while storing the interface MAC as source:

```c
if (eth_store_daddr(ctx, smac.addr, 0) < 0 ||
    eth_store_saddr(ctx, dmac.addr, 0) < 0)
    return DROP_WRITE_ERROR;
```

Finally it calls `redirect_self(ctx)`.

## `icmp6_send_ndisc_adv` (how `ICMP6_ND_OPT_LEN` is used)

`ICMP6_ND_OPT_LEN` is defined as `8`. In `icmp6_ndisc_adv_addopt`, it's used to extend the packet tail and increase the payload length when the NS lacks a source link-layer option:

```c
